---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { EMAILS } from '../config';

// Table of contents — ids must match the h2 ids below.
const toc = [
  { id: 'what-information-do-we-collect', title: 'What information do we collect?' },
  {
    id: 'sensitive-consumer-health-data',
    title: "Sensitive consumer health data: how we handle your child's care information",
  },
  { id: 'how-do-we-process-your-information', title: 'How do we process your information?' },
  {
    id: 'when-and-with-whom-do-we-share',
    title: 'When and with whom do we share your personal information?',
  },
  { id: 'cookies-and-tracking', title: 'Do we use cookies and other tracking technologies?' },
  { id: 'social-logins', title: 'How do we handle your social logins?' },
  { id: 'how-long-do-we-keep-your-information', title: 'How long do we keep your information?' },
  { id: 'how-do-we-keep-your-information-safe', title: 'How do we keep your information safe?' },
  { id: 'information-from-minors', title: 'Do we collect information from minors?' },
  { id: 'privacy-rights', title: 'What are your privacy rights?' },
  { id: 'do-not-track', title: 'Controls for Do-Not-Track features' },
  {
    id: 'us-privacy-rights',
    title: 'Do United States residents have specific privacy rights?',
  },
  { id: 'washington-my-health-my-data', title: 'Washington My Health My Data Act rights' },
  {
    id: 'gdpr',
    title: 'Do European Union residents have specific privacy rights (GDPR)?',
  },
  { id: 'shared-caregiver-access', title: 'Shared caregiver access' },
  { id: 'updates', title: 'Do we make updates to this notice?' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'How can you contact us about this notice?' },
  {
    id: 'review-update-delete',
    title: 'How can you review, update, or delete the data we collect from you?',
  },
];

const privacyEmail = EMAILS.privacy;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Handsful collects, uses, and protects your family's data."
  placeholder={false}
  noindex={true}
  lastUpdated="July 12, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Notice for MESQUITE &amp; THORN DIGITAL, LLC (doing business as Handsful)
    ("<strong>we</strong>," "<strong>us</strong>," or "<strong>our</strong>"), describes how and why
    we might access, collect, store, use, and/or share ("<strong>process</strong>") your personal
    information when you use our services ("<strong>Services</strong>"), including when you:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Visit our website at <a href="https://www.handsful.app">https://www.handsful.app</a> or any
      website of ours that links to this Privacy Notice
    </li>
    <li>Join our waitlist or subscribe to updates</li>
    <li>
      Download and use our mobile application (Handsful), once available, or any other application
      of ours that links to this Privacy Notice
    </li>
    <li>
      Use Handsful. Handsful is a mobile app that helps parents of multiples (twins, triplets, and
      more) log and track care activities for each of their children — including feeding, sleep,
      diaper changes, and growth — simultaneously across babies, compare activity side by side,
      share caregiver access with a partner or family member, and prepare notes for pediatrician
      visits. The app is intended for use by adults; it is not directed to children and is not
      intended to be used by children.
    </li>
    <li>Engage with us in other related ways, including any marketing or events</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Questions or concerns?</strong> Reading this Privacy Notice will help you understand
    your privacy rights and choices. We are responsible for making decisions about how your
    personal information is processed. If you do not agree with our policies and practices, please
    do not use our Services. If you still have any questions or concerns, please contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who-this-policy-is-about">A note on who this policy is about</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Notice describes both (1) how we handle information about you, the parent or
    caregiver who creates an account, and (2) how we handle information you provide about your
    child or children in the course of using the Services. Information about your children is
    provided by you, not collected directly from them, and is used solely to deliver the
    care-tracking features you've chosen to use.
  </p>

  <h2 id="summary-of-key-points">Summary of key points</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>What personal information do we process?</strong> When you visit, use, or navigate our
    Services, we may process personal information depending on how you interact with us and the
    Services, the choices you make, and the products and features you use. This includes
    information about your child or children that you choose to log. Learn more below.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Do we process any sensitive personal information?</strong> Yes. The care activity data
    you log about your child or children — including feeding, sleep, diaper, growth, and
    pediatrician visit information — is treated by us as sensitive consumer health data, and we
    apply heightened protections to it as described in this Notice.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Do we collect any information from third parties?</strong> We do not collect any
    information from third parties.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>How do we process your information?</strong> We process your information to provide,
    improve, and administer our Services, communicate with you, for security and fraud prevention,
    and to comply with law. We process sensitive consumer health data only with your affirmative
    consent, and only for the purposes you authorize. Learn more below.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>In what situations and with which parties do we share personal information?</strong>
    We may share information in specific situations and with specific third parties. We do not
    sell or share your sensitive consumer health data, and we do not use it for advertising. Learn
    more below.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>How do we keep your information safe?</strong> We have adequate organizational and
    technical processes and procedures in place to protect your personal information. However, no
    electronic transmission over the internet or information storage technology can be guaranteed
    to be 100% secure. Learn more below.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What are your rights?</strong> Depending on where you are located, applicable privacy
    law may give you certain rights regarding your personal information, including sensitive
    consumer health data. Learn more below.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>How do you exercise your rights?</strong> The easiest way to exercise your rights is
    by contacting us at <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>. We will consider
    and act upon any request in accordance with applicable data protection laws.
  </p>

  <h2 id="table-of-contents">Table of contents</h2>
  <ol class="toc">
    {
      toc.map(({ id, title }) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <h2 id="what-information-do-we-collect">1. What information do we collect?</h2>

  <h3>Personal information you disclose to us</h3>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: We collect personal information that you provide to us, including care information
      you choose to log about your child or children.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p>
    We collect personal information that you voluntarily provide to us when you register on the
    Services, join our waitlist, express interest in our products, or otherwise contact us.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Personal Information Provided by You.</strong> This may include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name</li>
    <li>Email address</li>
    <li>Password</li>
    <li>Contact and marketing preferences</li>
    <li>Your children's first names</li>
    <li>Your children's dates of birth (used to calculate age-appropriate tracking)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Sensitive Consumer Health Data.</strong> When you use the app (once available), you may
    log care activity data about your child or children, including: feeding times and amounts,
    sleep periods, diaper changes, growth measurements, and notes tagged for pediatrician visits.
    We treat this data as sensitive consumer health data. See
    <a href="#sensitive-consumer-health-data">Section 2</a> for how we handle it specifically.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Payment Data.</strong> If you subscribe to a paid tier, payment is handled by Apple,
    RevenueCat, and/or Google Play. We do not store your full payment card details. See their
    privacy notices:
    <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/</a
    >,
    <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy</a
    >,
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >https://policies.google.com/privacy</a
    >.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Social Media Login Data.</strong> If you register using Google Sign-In, we collect the
    profile information provided by that service, as described in
    <a href="#social-logins">Section 6</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Application Data.</strong> If you use the app, we may collect, with your permission,
    information from your mobile device such as device identifiers, model, operating system and
    version, and information about how you use app features. This is used to maintain security,
    troubleshoot issues, and for internal analytics.
  </p>

  <h3>Information automatically collected</h3>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: Some information, such as your IP address and device characteristics, is collected
      automatically when you visit the website.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p>
    When you visit the website, we automatically collect log and usage data (IP address, browser
    type, pages viewed, referring URLs) and device data. This does not, on its own, reveal your
    identity. See our Cookie Notice at
    <a href="/cookies">https://www.handsful.app/cookies</a> for details on tracking technologies
    used on the website.
  </p>

  <h3>Google API</h3>
  <p>
    Our use of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the
    <a
      href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a
    >, including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sensitive-consumer-health-data">
    2. Sensitive consumer health data: how we handle your child's care information
  </h2>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: Feeding, sleep, diaper, growth, and pediatrician visit data you log about your
      child is sensitive consumer health data. We collect it only with your consent, use it only
      to provide the Services you request, and do not sell it or use it for advertising.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p>
    Because Handsful is built around logging care activities for infants and young children, much
    of the data you enter is, or is closely related to, health information about a minor. We apply
    the following commitments to this category of data specifically:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>We collect this data only when you affirmatively choose to log it.</li>
    <li>We do not sell this data.</li>
    <li>We do not share this data for the purposes of targeted advertising.</li>
    <li>We do not use geofencing around health care facilities in connection with this data.</li>
    <li>
      Access to this data within our systems is limited to what is necessary to provide the
      Services (for example, syncing your entries across your devices and to caregivers you've
      invited).
    </li>
    <li>
      Where we use third-party infrastructure providers to store or process this data (see
      <a href="#when-and-with-whom-do-we-share">Section 4</a>), those providers are contractually
      restricted from using it for any purpose other than providing services to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may delete individual entries or your full account's data at any time from within the
      app. See <a href="#review-update-delete">Section 18</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If we ever introduce features that process this data using artificial intelligence or machine
    learning tools (for example, AI-generated visit-prep summaries), we will update this Privacy
    Notice to describe that processing, name the provider involved, and obtain any additional
    consent required by law before that feature is enabled for your account.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-do-we-process-your-information">3. How do we process your information?</h2>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: We process your information to provide, improve, and administer the Services,
      communicate with you, for security and fraud prevention, and to comply with law.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p>We process personal information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Create and maintain your account and authenticate you</li>
    <li>Deliver the care-tracking, comparison, and caregiver-sharing features you use</li>
    <li>Respond to support inquiries</li>
    <li>Send administrative information about the Services</li>
    <li>
      Send marketing communications, where you've opted in (see
      <a href="#privacy-rights">Section 10</a>)
    </li>
    <li>Protect the Services, including fraud monitoring</li>
    <li>Understand usage trends and improve the Services</li>
    <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not use your child's care data to make automated decisions that produce legal or
    similarly significant effects, and we do not use it to train third-party AI models.
  </p>

  <h2 id="when-and-with-whom-do-we-share">
    4. When and with whom do we share your personal information?
  </h2>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: We share information only with service providers who need it to operate the
      Services, under contract, and never for advertising purposes involving sensitive consumer
      health data.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p><strong>Currently live (website):</strong></p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Category</th>
          <th scope="col">Provider</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Website hosting</td>
          <td>Vercel</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Email list / marketing (waitlist)</td>
          <td>Kit (ConvertKit)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Web analytics</td>
          <td>Google Analytics (GA4) — active only after you consent via our cookie banner</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p><strong>Planned for app launch:</strong></p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Category</th>
          <th scope="col">Provider</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>User account registration and authentication</td>
          <td>Firebase Authentication</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>App data storage and sync</td>
          <td>Cloud Firestore / Firebase</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Subscription billing</td>
          <td>RevenueCat, Apple, Google Play</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Cloud infrastructure</td>
          <td>Google Cloud Platform</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    We will update this table as additional providers are added, and will note here if any future
    provider will have access to sensitive consumer health data.
  </p>
  <p>
    We also may need to share your personal information in connection with a merger, sale of
    company assets, financing, or acquisition of all or part of our business — sensitive consumer
    health data will remain subject to the protections in this Notice through any such transfer.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies-and-tracking">5. Do we use cookies and other tracking technologies?</h2>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: We use cookies and similar technologies on the website for functionality and, with
      your consent, for analytics.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p>
    We use essential cookies to operate the website. With your consent, given through our cookie
    banner, we also use Google Analytics to understand website usage. GA4 does not collect or
    process any information from within the app itself, and never processes your child's care
    data.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can withdraw consent to analytics cookies at any time through the cookie preferences link
    in the website footer. See our Cookie Notice at
    <a href="/cookies">https://www.handsful.app/cookies</a> for full details.
  </p>

  <h2 id="social-logins">6. How do we handle your social logins?</h2>
  <p>
    If you register using Google Sign-In, we receive certain profile information (such as name and
    email address) from Google, used only for the purposes described in this Notice. We recommend
    reviewing Google's privacy notice to understand their own data practices.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-long-do-we-keep-your-information">7. How long do we keep your information?</h2>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: We keep your information for as long as you have an account, unless a longer
      period is required by law.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p>
    We retain personal information, including care activity data, for as long as your account is
    active. When you delete your account, we delete or anonymize your data, except where retention
    is required for legal, tax, or fraud-prevention purposes, or where data exists in backup
    archives, in which case we isolate it from further processing until deletion is possible.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-do-we-keep-your-information-safe">8. How do we keep your information safe?</h2>
  <p>
    We implement reasonable technical and organizational security measures designed to protect
    personal information, including sensitive consumer health data. No method of transmission or
    storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2 id="information-from-minors">9. Do we collect information from minors?</h2>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: Handsful is designed for use by parents and caregivers 18 years of age or older.
      We do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not direct the Services to children and do not knowingly collect personal information
    directly from a child. Parents and caregivers may log information about their children —
    including first name, date of birth, and care activity data — but this is provided by the
    parent or caregiver, not the child, and is used solely to deliver the tracking features within
    the parent's account. If you believe we have inadvertently collected information directly from
    a child, contact us at <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a> and we will
    promptly address it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="privacy-rights">10. What are your privacy rights?</h2>
  <p>
    You may withdraw consent, opt out of marketing communications, and review, update, or delete
    your account information at any time. See
    <a href="#review-update-delete">Section 18</a> for how to exercise these rights. Sensitive
    consumer health data can be deleted at the individual entry level or in bulk via account
    deletion within the app.
  </p>

  <h2 id="do-not-track">11. Controls for Do-Not-Track features</h2>
  <p>
    There is currently no uniform standard for DNT signals, so we do not respond to them at this
    time. If a legal standard is adopted, we will update this Notice accordingly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="us-privacy-rights">12. Do United States residents have specific privacy rights?</h2>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: Residents of California, Colorado, Connecticut, and other states with
      comprehensive privacy laws have rights to know, access, correct, delete, and opt out of
      certain processing of their personal information, including sensitive personal information.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p><strong>Categories of Personal Information We Collect (past 12 months):</strong></p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Category</th>
          <th scope="col">Examples</th>
          <th scope="col">Collected</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>A. Identifiers</td>
          <td>Name, email, IP address, account name</td>
          <td>YES</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>B. California Customer Records</td>
          <td>Name, contact info, financial information</td>
          <td>YES</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>F. Internet/network activity</td>
          <td>Website browsing and interaction data</td>
          <td>YES</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sensitive personal information</td>
          <td>Consumer health data (your child's care activity data)</td>
          <td>YES</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    We have not sold your personal information, including sensitive personal information, in the
    preceding twelve months. We do not use sensitive consumer health data for cross-context
    behavioral advertising.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your rights include the right to know, access, correct, delete, obtain a copy of, and opt out
    of certain processing of your personal information, including the right to limit use of
    sensitive personal information under California law. To exercise these rights, contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="washington-my-health-my-data">13. Washington My Health My Data Act rights</h2>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: If you are a Washington resident, or your consumer health data was collected in
      Washington, you have specific rights under the My Health My Data Act.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p>
    We treat the care activity data logged in Handsful (feeding, sleep, diaper, growth, and
    pediatrician visit notes) as "consumer health data" under the Washington My Health My Data
    Act. In addition to the rights described elsewhere in this Notice, Washington residents have
    the right to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Confirm whether we are collecting, sharing, or selling their consumer health data, and to
      access that data
    </li>
    <li>Withdraw consent to our collection or sharing of their consumer health data</li>
    <li>Have their consumer health data deleted</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We obtain your consent before collecting consumer health data, do not sell it, and do not
    share it for advertising purposes. To exercise these rights, contact
    <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>. You may also submit complaints to the
    Washington State Attorney General.
  </p>

  <h2 id="gdpr">14. Do European Union residents have specific privacy rights (GDPR)?</h2>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: If you are located in the EU/EEA or UK, you have rights under the GDPR, including
      for special category data such as your child's health-related information.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p>
    Where GDPR applies, our legal basis for processing your account information is performance of
    a contract with you (providing the Services) and, for marketing, your consent. Our legal basis
    for processing your child's care activity data is your explicit consent, given at the point
    you enable tracking features.
  </p>
  <p>
    You have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict, or port your data, and to withdraw
    consent at any time without affecting the lawfulness of processing before withdrawal. To
    exercise these rights, contact <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>. You may
    also lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2 id="shared-caregiver-access">15. Shared caregiver access</h2>
  <p class="in-short">
    <em>
      In Short: If you invite another caregiver to your account, they will be able to view and add
      to your child's care data. If that caregiver's access is later removed, the entries they
      logged remain in your child's record, but you can choose to anonymize the label showing who
      logged them.
    </em>
  </p>
  <p>
    Handsful allows you to share access to your child's tracking data with another caregiver (such
    as a co-parent or family member) that you invite. Once invited and accepted, that caregiver
    can view and log entries for your child, including sensitive consumer health data, subject to
    the permissions you grant. You are responsible for deciding who to invite.
  </p>
  <p>When a caregiver's access is removed:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Entries they logged remain part of your child's record — we do not delete a removed
      caregiver's past entries, since they form part of your child's ongoing care history.
    </li>
    <li>
      By default, entries stay attributed to the caregiver who logged them. You may choose to
      anonymize the visible label (for example, showing "Caregiver 2" instead of a name) without
      deleting the underlying entries.
    </li>
    <li>
      We retain an internal record of the true attribution (which caregiver logged which entry)
      for up to 12 months after a caregiver's access is removed, restricted to internal use for
      security, dispute resolution, and legal compliance purposes. This internal record is not
      visible to you, other caregivers, or the removed caregiver through the app.
    </li>
    <li>
      A removed caregiver may request deletion of their personal information, including this
      internal attribution record, as described in
      <a href="#privacy-rights">Section 10</a> (or
      <a href="#washington-my-health-my-data">Section 13</a> for Washington residents, or
      <a href="#gdpr">Section 14</a> for EU/EEA and UK residents). Deletion of the internal
      attribution record does not delete the underlying care entries themselves, which remain
      part of your child's record.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To revoke a caregiver's access, use in-app account management once available, or contact us
    at <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="updates">16. Do we make updates to this notice?</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Notice from time to time, indicated by the "Last updated" date above.
    Material changes will be communicated by prominent notice or direct notification before they
    take effect.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">17. How can you contact us about this notice?</h2>
  <p>
    MESQUITE &amp; THORN DIGITAL, LLC<br />
    Data Protection Officer<br />
    1018 E Washington St, Suite A<br />
    Brownsville, TX 78520<br />
    United States<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="review-update-delete">
    18. How can you review, update, or delete the data we collect from you?
  </h2>
  <p>
    You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information, including
    your child's care activity data, by contacting
    <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a> or, once available, through account
    settings within the app.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>

<style>
  /* TOC anchor targets must clear the sticky header (48px logo + padding). */
  h2 {
